</p>

<p>Simple homemade <strong>Eggs Benedict</strong>:</p>

<ul>
  <li>Toasted base (bread / muffin)</li>
  <li>Poached egg</li>
  <li>A slice of ham or smoked salmon</li>
  <li>Hollandaise sauce on top</li>
</ul>

<hr />

<h2 id="hollandaise-very-roughly">Hollandaise, very roughly</h2>

<p>A basic hollandaise is just <strong>egg yolk + butter + acid</strong>:</p>

<ol>
  <li>Whisk egg yolks with a bit of lemon juice (and a splash of water) in a heatproof bowl.</li>
  <li>Set the bowl over gentle steam (not boiling water), keep whisking until it slightly thickens.</li>
  <li>Slowly drizzle in melted butter while whisking constantly, until it turns smooth and creamy.</li>
  <li>Season with salt, pepper, and a bit more lemon juice if needed.</li>
</ol>

<p>Then just pour it over the poached egg and eat before it cools down.
